00:02:42,780 --> 00:02:52,180
And iron is when the iron is bound to a molecule that is kind of keeping it from being in a chemical

00:02:52,180 --> 00:02:55,060
state where it is reactive.

00:02:55,060 --> 00:03:00,780
So an example of bound iron would be the hemoglobin.

00:03:00,780 --> 00:03:09,860
So iron is bound to that hemoglobin within the blood, so it's not chemically reactive.

00:03:09,860 --> 00:03:13,700
And then another example would be ferritin.

00:03:13,700 --> 00:03:18,300
So within the cells, ferritin is holding onto that iron.

00:03:18,300 --> 00:03:24,460
So when it's bound, it's being held until the body needs to utilize those sources.

00:03:24,460 --> 00:03:29,220
So that is the proper way we want to have iron within the body.

00:03:29,220 --> 00:03:36,180
